"{\n  \"url\": \"http://localhost:3001/daily-briefs/6eaec0e0-cdce-4bd5-b6df-f7378ce2759a\",\n  \"text\": \"PROJECT\\nAlleato AI\\nCompany Directory\\nCOMPANY-WIDE TOOLS\\nAlleato AI\\nCompany\\nCompany Directory\\nUser Management\\nMeetings\\nTasks\\nDocumentation\\nEstimates\\nPrime Contracts\\nChange Events\\nPotential Change Orders\\nAdmin Dashboard\\nCompany\\nDaily Briefs\\n6eaec0e0 Cdce 4bd5 B6df F7378ce2759a\\nSelect Project\\nCompany\\nDaily Executive Brief - 2026-07-06\\nBUSINESS DAY\\n2026-07-06\\nPACKET STATE\\ncurrent\\nSOURCES\\n212\\nGENERATED\\nJul 7, 2026, 1:32 AM\\nSource of truth: `intelligence_packets` / `daily-executive-brief`\\nEXECUTIVE READ\\n\\nMain owner exposure today is **execution discipline plus a few real project blockers**. The most immediate job risk is the **rack/sprinkler/hazmat bracket path**: rack readiness is still pegged to a hard worst-case **7/10**, a lift install error already caused rework, and hazmat bracket sourcing remains unresolved and could delay closeout if not escalated now [01KW9HBHD8S5PZBH5RB39F0328].\\n\\nSecond, **client-facing schedule certainty is thin on multiple jobs**: UQ Philipsburg still lacks a formal remaining schedule and has a hard owner constraint of **no Skypod disruption** unless an alternate approach is used [outlook_AAMkADAwNzg3ZTA5LTJmMWEtNDczNi04ODcxLTk1MTA1ODhmYmIyNABGAAAAAAAU1WTKtGciQa9go1eRAG9JBwD__y9hPlJRRYxFT5QN_MgoAAAAAAEMAAD__y9hPlJRRYxFT5QN_MgoAARKD96wAAA=, outlook_AAMkADBjMWMyYWI1LWE4ZjAtNDUwMy04NzBmLWYyN2Q3MDg0ZDU2ZgBGAAAAAACGVNWcC9x6TZ3hpX2q-XxPBwDu9QOyYKZbS5NACM9H9erIAAAAAAEMAADu9QOyYKZbS5NACM9H9erIAADv1YpbAAA=]. McLane Exotec permitting is also behind and may expose **out-of-scope fire work** [outlook_AAMkADAwNzg3ZTA5LTJmMWEtNDczNi04ODcxLTk1MTA1ODhmYmIyNABGAAAAAAAU1WTKtGciQa9go1eRAG9JBwD__y9hPlJRRYxFT5QN_MgoAAAAAAEMAAD__y9hPlJRRYxFT5QN_MgoAARKD964AAA=, outlook_AAMkADAwNzg3ZTA5LTJmMWEtNDczNi04ODcxLTk1MTA1ODhmYmIyNABGAAAAAAAU1WTKtGciQa9go1eRAG9JBwD__y9hPlJRRYxFT5QN_MgoAAAAAAEMAAD__y9hPlJRRYxFT5QN_MgoAARKD97UAAA=].\\n\\nOperationally, leadership is correctly tying **missed communication/follow-through to direct cost**, with cited exposure of **$10k+ per incident** and discussion of **$300k/year** avoidable loss [01KWVK2M7QE21FXYB1NAHPY1GB]. That risk is not abstract; it shows up across delayed permitting, incomplete estimating, and procurement gaps.\\n\\nCRITICAL DECISIONS NEEDED\\n**Hazmat bracket escalation:** authorize immediate escalation path beyond normal calls if Jason remains unresponsive; current plan already contemplates local office visit and alternate local vendor outreach [01KW9HBHD8S5PZBH5RB39F0328].\\n**UQ Philipsburg execution choice:** force a yes/no on whether zero-disruption tie-in is truly guaranteed; if not, direct team to price/advance **option-B** now instead of waiting [outlook_AAMkADAwNzg3ZTA5LTJmMWEtNDczNi04ODcxLTk1MTA1ODhmYmIyNABGAAAAAAAU1WTKtGciQa9go1eRAG9JBwD__y9hPlJRRYxFT5QN_MgoAAAAAAEMAAD__y9hPlJRRYxFT5QN_MgoAARKD96wAAA=, outlook_AAMkADk2MTgxYzJhLTUzZjctNDIzZS05ZDkxLTg2NTcyNTRiOWRhYQBGAAAAAAC44Z9cGTA6SKuHAQ6MZsBABwDEL6z4g2_XQZJZM15izKp5AAAAAAEMAADEL6z4g2_XQZJZM15izKp5AAEmuRrKAAA=].\\n**Pensacola RFQ clarifications:** domes\",\n  \"hasTitle\": true,\n  \"hasSot\": true,\n  \"hasSources\": true,\n  \"hasDecisions\": false\n}"
